Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the SBG-Website project.

## Implementation Summary

This project is built with React + Vite, and I followed the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) to implement the analytics integration.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration (src/App.tsx)
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to both application states:
  - Logged-out state: Added inside `<BrowserRouter>` for public pages (Login, Landing, About, Clubs & Committees)
  - Logged-in state: Added inside `<BrowserRouter>` for authenticated pages (Dashboard, Booking, Admin pages, etc.)
- Component placement ensures analytics tracking works across all routes in the application

## Framework-Specific Implementation
Following Vercel's official documentation for React/Vite projects:
- Used the React-specific package: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component as per React best practices
- No additional configuration required for Vite

## Next Steps for Full Activation
To complete the setup and start collecting analytics data:
1. Deploy this updated code to Vercel
2. In your Vercel dashboard, navigate to the Analytics section
3. Select your project and click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. After deployment, verify analytics are working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✅ All existing functionality preserved
- ✅ Analytics component added to all routes (logged-in and logged-out)

The implementation is production-ready and follows Vercel's official guidelines for React + Vite applications.
